language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Minimum number of 8-hour bus shifts over six 4-hour time slots of a day, cyclic, so that each slot's demand is met.
given demands : matrix indexed by [int(1..6)] of int(0..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..6)] of int(0..100)

branching on [x]
minimising (sum i : int(1..6) . x[i])
such that
$ each bus works 8 successive hours, so it covers its start slot and the next slot (the day wraps around)
$ the number of buses available in each 4-hour interval meets the demand for that interval
forAll i : int(1..6) . ((x[i] + x[(i+4)%6+1]) >= demands[i])
